 shared read-ahead/offline reader.\n- Zero processor latency/tail; float headroom and existing resource/RT boundaries preserved.\n- Strict schema1.9 and neutral migration from1.0–1.8; invalid types, keys, curves, values and overflow refuse.\n- Exact canonical doubles survive untouched rounded locale controls. Structural clip controls stay read-only during prepared audio until live generation/events are implemented.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Local Release12 selected tests; original analytic/reference-independent samples and actual captured 1/2/8/32/256-channel live/export equality, overlap, split/trim, history and Save/reopen. Core185303 checks.\n- Actual offscreen StudioWindow workflow, locale/precision/wheel/read-only controls and screenshot. UI readiness fixture failure is retained and fixed by waiting for visible state; guards unchanged.\n- ASan/UBSan7 selected tests pass (leak detection disabled).\n- Prior PR72 final repaired qualification retained separately: exact cca9735/merge tree, Linux90/native Windows core26/Qt7, API/archive digests and source/evidence hashes.\n- Expands native Windows core and Qt CI to the new concrete workflows without changing the four required contexts.\n\n## Limits and next task\n\nPartial P009 implementation, no F/Q/C/N promotion. Independent source/project timing, qualified rate/stretch/pitch, linked interactive crossfades/comp/warp and live clip automation remain. Then explicit import conversion/loss preview, grouped acceptance/Undo/reopen, aligned source-suite renders and refreshed installed preview pairs.\n\nOfficial-source resampler/stretch candidate/license review and a bounded already-installed Linux four-tone probe are retained; no dependency adopted. No VM, device audio, system install, equalizer checkout or public product release changed.\n\n## Retained first hosted failure and repair\n\nFirst head b1a4c30 passed Windows cross-build/core28/Qt8. Linux91/92 refused the8192-track viewport fixture because schema1.9's conservative canonical preflight exceeded its64MiB grant. The fixture now declares96MiB, explicitly tests unchanged64MiB refusal and preserves the8192-track viewport, history and raw-media assertions. Local affected Release3 tests pass. Production defaults/quotas are unchanged. Source-appropriate native/full CI is required again. The focused-Undo exploratory case passed; no production defect/refresh change was introduced. All first-head archives/API digests and the actual refusal are retained.\n\n## Native focused-Undo reproduction and production repair\n\nSecond head e6d4eda passes Linux92 and native core28/cross-build. Native Windows Qt7/8 exposes stale canonical display after focused Undo (line187), after focus is successfully assigned. The actual failure and all artifact digests are retained. Production refresh now compares the selected clip's stored processing; changed settings update its fields even while focused. Unrelated publication keeps ordinary focused input. The assertion and timeout remain intact; local Release6 affected tests pass. Current-source native/full gates are required again.\n\nA local8192-track ASan/UBSan viewport run timed out at its existing180-second limit;2/3 tests passed. The timeout remains recorded, with no retry/deadline increase and no inferred cause. The preceding7/7 sanitizer cohort retains its own exact scope.\n\nCurrent repair also passes three affected desktop ASan/UBSan tests in5.91s\n(leak detection disabled). Six affected Release tests pass in9.72s. The inspected\nowned1100×850 screenshot is retained. This scope does not erase the separate\nlarge-project sanitizer timeout or establish new installed/native qualification.\n\n## Final repaired qualification and protected merge\n\nExact head 1849bde9a588cb2d05cd6429a997371e2dba9707 / run37928624392 passed all four unchanged required\ncontexts: Linux92, native Windows core28, native Qt8, plus the cross-build.\nNative Qt passes the unchanged focused-Undo assertion. Three archives were\nverified against GitHub SHA256 digests and exact raw LastTest bytes.\nMerge 2882f11b2a9dc6817132a1252a63dfbf4a45200f has the identical tested tree; no bypass. Twenty source and\n87 committed evidence hashes were verified against the merged tree.\n[Exact qualified run](https://github.com/rhamenator/soundcurrent-daw/actions/runs/37928624392).\n\nThe separate large-project sanitizer timeout remains open; affected repaired\ndesktop Release6 and ASan/UBSan3 pass with leak detection disabled. No installed\npreview refresh or native audio qualification is inferred. Packaging is deferred\nwhile host disk contention remains high; the prior local package is older source\nand lacks the focused-control repair. No VM, physical audio route, system install,\nequalizer checkout or public product release changed. Full frozen parity remains\nincomplete.\n","created_at":"2026-10-09T11:35:32Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T12:25:29Z","closed_at":"2026-10-09T12:24:10Z","merged_at":"2026-10-09T12:24:10Z","merge_commit_sha":"2882f11b2a9dc6817132a1252a63dfbf4a45200f","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rhamenator/soundcurrent-daw/pulls/73/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rhamenator/soundcurrent-daw/pulls/73/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rhamenator/soundcurrent-daw/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rhamenator/soundcurrent-daw/issues/73/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rhamenator/soundcurrent-daw/statuses/1849bde9a588cb2d05cd6429a997371e2dba9707","head":{"label":"rhamenator:codex/clip-envelopes","ref":"codex/clip-envelopes","sha":"1849bde9a588cb2d05cd6429a997371e2dba9707","user":{"login":"rhamenator","id":51587867,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNTg3ODY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51587867?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rhamenator","ht